{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791797337,"nonce":"3FBBsUOUCCGmGtXbkq3Q1DOW9P0=","title":"Generic calls through enum parameters erase the caller type argument","message":"The same generic leaf-reading function works when called directly on Value\u003cFloat\u003e, but fails when readOuter\u003cT\u003e(Nested\u003cT\u003e):T destructures Wrap(inner) and calls read(inner). Native Haxe passes both Float and String checks; Rayzor v55 fails the Float branch value assertion.\n\nMIR infer_generic_call_args only pairs bare parameters and Array elements. It does not descend through Enum\u003cT\u003e, Class\u003cT\u003e or other nominal type arguments. In a generic caller the AST inference also skips actual TypeParameter arguments. The emitted inner call has no explicit type arguments; monomorphization treats the callee as unbound and installs an I64 specialization before the caller is specialized. The GadtEvaluation probe extracted from TestGADT shows evalConst__i64 and eval__i64__f64 where a forwarded T or C is required.\n\nReproducer (haxe --interp passes; rayzor run --release --preset application --tier 1 --tier-start-interpreted false --tier-promotion false fails):\n\nimport haxe.macro.Context;\nusing haxe.macro.TypeTools;\nprivate enum Value\u003cT\u003e {\n    TextValue(value:String):Value\u003cString\u003e;\n    FloatValue(value:String):Value\u003cFloat\u003e;\n    IntValue(value:String):Value\u003cInt\u003e;\n}\nprivate enum Nested\u003cT\u003e { Wrap(value:Value\u003cT\u003e); }\nclass GadtRecursive {\n    static function read\u003cT\u003e(value:Value\u003cT\u003e):T {\n        return switch (value) {\n            case TextValue(text): text;\n            case FloatValue(text): Std.parseFloat(text);\n            case IntValue(text): Std.parseInt(text);\n        };\n    }\n    static function readOuter\u003cT\u003e(value:Nested\u003cT\u003e):T {\n        return switch (value) { case Wrap(inner): read(inner); };\n    }\n    static macro function same(value:haxe.macro.Expr, expected:haxe.macro.Expr):haxe.macro.Expr {\n        return macro $v{Context.typeof(value).toString() == Context.typeof(expected).toString()};\n    }\n    static function main() {\n        if (!same(read(FloatValue(\"2.5\")), (null:Float))) throw \"result type\";\n        if (readOuter(Wrap(FloatValue(\"2.5\"))) != 2.5) throw \"float branch value\";\n        if (readOuter(Wrap(TextValue(\"two\"))) != \"two\") throw \"string branch value\";\n        trace(\"CONFORMANCE_OK\");\n    }\n}","files":null}]}